---
import PortfolioDetail from '../layouts/PortfolioDetail.astro';
---

<PortfolioDetail title="Scotiabank Projects">
  <!-- Introduction + Logo Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
        <!-- Intro text: 8/12 on desktop -->
        <div class="md:col-span-8">
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 mb-12 md:mb-0">
            <p class="text-xl">
              During my time at Scotiabank, I worked on a range of applications and features across the capital-markets space. Because of bank policy, I’m not able to share screenshots or detailed visuals in my portfolio, but I’m always happy to talk about them in person. Here are a few projects that might be of interest.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Logo: 4/12 on desktop, below text on mobile -->
        <div class="md:col-span-4 flex justify-center md:justify-end">
          <img src="/scotia/scotiabank-logo.png" alt="Scotiabank Logo" class="w-40 md:w-56 h-auto" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Projects List Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="space-y-12">
        <!-- Project 1 -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border-b border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-bold text-xl mb-3">GC Mobile Solution via Edge</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
             A mobile-forward web app designed to help the Sales team book RFQs with support from the Structuring team. It was built to replace long, messy email threads and streamline the booking workflow. (Easily my favourite project.)
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 2 -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border-b border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-bold text-xl mb-3">S/N Pre-Issuance RFQ Web Application</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            A browser-based tool that lets users submit and manage RFQ requests more efficiently, reducing back-and-forth and keeping everything in a single, trackable place.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 3 -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border-b border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-bold text-xl mb-3">Client Value System (CVS)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            A redesign and migration of a legacy platform that measures a client’s financial value and long-term potential. The work focused on modernizing the interface while keeping the complex underlying logic intact.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 4 -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border-b border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-bold text-xl mb-3">Structuring Tool</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
             A trade-creation interface for the Structuring team. It allowed users to assemble OTC trades by selecting fields, conditions, and pricing details: a flexible “build your own ticket” concept.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 5 -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border-b border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-bold text-xl mb-3">Data Dictionary Management Tool</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            An internal system for managing data types and adding new fields to trade tickets, helping teams maintain consistency and handle updates without relying on manual processes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Call to Action Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        If you'd like to dig into any of these, just ask me during the interview.<br />
        I can share much more context there.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PortfolioDetail>
